      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Your observation about sudden, lagging movements differs from the gradual effects of fatigue, and while it sounds like a software glitch, human causes like occasional dizziness or reading glasses can create similar moments of unusual movement. It is also possible that video recording at lower frame rates during a stressful event can inadvertently capture mechanical-looking pauses in facial expressions. Ultimately, without technical footage or professional analysis, we can't confirm a peculiarity beyond standard interpretive exaggeration of a human expression.",
